<section image-layout="blank"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item padding="32pt 48pt 20pt"><p role="eyebrow">The navigator’s clock</p><h2>Minutes, then hundreds of thousands of years</h2><p font-size="18pt">Expansion cools the universe. Conditions change long before the first stars shine.</p><custom-code><div style="height:220pt;width:100%"><svg viewBox="0 0 850 230" width="100%" height="100%" role="img" aria-label="Logarithmic cosmic timeline: early minutes, 380000 years, hundreds of millions of years, and 13.8 billion years today"><line x1="24" y1="112" x2="823" y2="112" stroke="#73DDE7" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M70 111 Q240 45 400 111" fill="none" stroke="#E8BC67" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 7"/><text x="245" y="75" text-anchor="middle" fill="#E8BC67" font-size="17">The clock speeds up across the chart</text><g fill="#F4F0DF" font-family="sans-serif" font-size="18"><text x="5" y="29">FIRST MINUTES</text><text x="5" y="54">Lightweight nuclei form</text><text x="460" y="29">≈380,000 YEARS</text><text x="460" y="54">Atoms form; light travels freely</text><text x="593" y="175">HUNDREDS OF MILLIONS</text><text x="593" y="200">The first stars shine</text><text x="824" y="87" text-anchor="end" font-size="16">13.8 billion · today</text></g><g stroke="#E8BC67" stroke-width="2"><line x1="45" y1="65" x2="45" y2="112"/><line x1="594" y1="65" x2="594" y2="112"/><line x1="740" y1="115" x2="740" y2="150"/></g><g fill="#E8BC67"><circle cx="45" cy="112" r="7"/><circle cx="594" cy="112" r="7"/><rect x="715" y="104" width="50" height="16" rx="8"/><circle cx="823" cy="112" r="5"/></g><g fill="#73DDE7" font-family="sans-serif" font-size="13"><text x="18" y="141">minutes</text><text x="309" y="141">1 year</text><text x="558" y="141">100,000 years</text></g></svg></div></custom-code><p font-size="16pt"><b>A logarithmic course:</b> equal horizontal gaps multiply the age; they do not add equal years. The star band indicates a broad era, not a measured uncertainty interval.</p><p role="caption"><span text-color="palette-4">Early minutes and first-star era are approximate. Source: </span><a href="https://science.nasa.gov/universe/overview/">NASA · Universe Overview</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>